      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_3",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("Welcome back! This is the second part of the two-part tutorial. Part 2 will teach you about recalling units, abilities and weapon specials, income and upkeep, long-distance movement, zone of control, and time of day."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("Ho, Galdrad! Has Delfador conjured something else to beat me with? A flock of scarecrows, perhaps?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("What should I do?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to_unit",
            id: "Dumbo",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("First, we will have to deal with the Orcish Grunt stationed in the middle of the river. He should be little trouble."),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to_unit",
            id: "Thrag",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("By then, their leader will have recruited more units to send against us and the real fight will begin."),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to",
            x: 14,
            y: 3,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("See this dark blue water? It’s too deep for either side to cross. The orcs could slowly wade through that narrow band of shallow lighter-blue water in the north; but we could stand on the shore and force them to fight us from the water, where they are exposed and we are protected by the forest."),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to",
            x: 16,
            y: 10,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("The more likely attack, then, is across the bridge. That middle island is the key: it has a village for healing injured units and forests in which we fight so well."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("Let’s go! Attack!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("You also have two new types of units to recruit this scenario: Elvish Archers and Elvish Shamans. I’ll tell you more about them when you recruit them. Personally, I would recommend a balanced force of two archers, two fighters, and a shaman."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_4",
        on: "recruit",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "predicate",
                name: "wml_filter",
                unit: "$last_recruit_id",
                filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22filter%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22side%22%3A%221%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22Elvish%20Shaman%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "$unit.profile",
            text: _("The Shaman has the ability to <i>heal</i> friendly units around her. She also has a special attack which <i>slows</i> enemies, halving the damage they do for one turn. However, she’s physically weaker than fighters and archers, so be careful when sending her into battle."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("At the start of each turn, allied units adjacent to a Shaman will recover 4 hitpoints, which is only half of the amount that a village would provide. The Shaman doesn’t gain experience from healing, only from combat, but advancing her is worthwhile — her second-level Elvish Druid advancement has healing equivalent to a village. A detailed explanation of healing may be found in the <i>Gameplay</i> section of the help (default hotkey: <b>F1</b>)."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("Weapon specials are special attack modifiers that make certain attacks more powerful. In this case, the Shaman has the Slows special on her entangle attack. When this attack successfully hits an enemy, it will halve the damage they do for one turn. Other weapon specials include First Strike, which allows that attack to always hit first no matter who attacks first, and Magical, which gives that attack a constant 70% chance to hit. A full list of abilities and weapon specials, along with traits, may be found in the help (default hotkey: <b>F1</b>)."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_5",
        on: "recruit",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "predicate",
                name: "wml_filter",
                unit: "$last_recruit_id",
                filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22filter%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22side%22%3A%221%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22Elvish%20Shaman%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "have_unit",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "$unit.profile",
            text: _("A unit in a village will receive healing from the village instead of from adjacent healers."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("Having more than one healer allows them to heal each other or to cover separate areas of the battlefield. It can also allow better tactical movement — the 2 hitpoints from rest-healing does combine with other sources of healing, so it’s often better to move a healer instead of an injured unit."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_6",
        on: "recruit",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "predicate",
                name: "wml_filter",
                unit: "$last_recruit_id",
                filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22filter%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22side%22%3A%221%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22Elvish%20Archer%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "$unit.profile",
            text: _("Unlike the Elvish Fighter, which has strong melee attacks, the Elvish Archer has strong ranged attacks. It’s useful to attack enemy units with strong melee attacks with strong ranged attacks, and vice versa. This allows your units to take less damage overall when your enemy counterattacks."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_7_1",
        on: "recruit",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "predicate",
                name: "wml_filter",
                unit: "$last_recruit_id",
                filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22filter%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22side%22%3A%221%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "variable",
                name: "turn_number",
              },
              {
                tag: "have_unit",
                side: 1,
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("You certainly have a fondness for shamans, I see. They will provide a lot of healing, but not much offensive potential."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("While none of your recruited units can move yet, you still can. You need more income; there are some villages near the keep you can capture."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
