          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "variable",
                name: "turn_number",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_12",
        on: "turn",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "turn_number",
            equals: 2,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("Galdrad, if I go by the ford, I could sneak up near his keep and dispatch him quickly."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("You could. However, elves (and orcs) have bad <i>defense</i> in water. You’ll be more vulnerable as you try to wade slowly across the ford; the enemy will have an 80% chance to hit you. Since elves have good defense in the forest, I would advise you keep to the trees and attack the orcs from there; your Fighters will only suffer a 40% chance of being hit in return, while Shamans and Archers will only incur a 30% chance."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("However, keep an eye on that ford. The orcs may try to sneak around behind our forces. It might do to send a few units to defend the banks, and the village there."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("Alright. The bridge it is, then, but I’ll be careful about the crossing."),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to_unit",
            id: "Dumbo",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("That Orcish Grunt is still blocking our path. He has no ranged attacks, so your archers should be able to engage him with little risk. Unfortunately, your units cannot reach him this turn, but you should not let them languish! Move them into position so they can attack next turn. There are also other villages on this side of the river. You should secure them for income and healing."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("I think I’ll stick around the keep for now, in order to recruit more units."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_13",
        on: "side_turn_end",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "turn_side",
            equals: 2,
          },
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "turn_number",
            equals: 2,
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_16",
        on: "branch_if_16",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "unit.id",
            equals: "student",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "student",
            text: _("I hope I will survive the counter-attack if my units can’t take this grunt out this turn. I should order them to grab more villages if they can and move everyone closer for next turn."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Galdrad",
            text: _("If one of your Shamans stands just behind you, she will heal you 4 hitpoints at the beginning of the next turn."),
          },
        ],
